Management cluster mgmt/mgmt
  record   mer-management  one bootstrap profile per variant (4), fetching its release from the gateway

In ConfigHub
  5 Targets in mer-targets, one per cluster, on a server-hosted worker
  1 component, each one base, 3 class bases, 4 variants, 1 management record
  10 Spaces and 7 Links, one tying each variant to its base (check your organization's quotas for both first)
  first rollout: kyverno in 3 stages after its class bases; one approval per stage, one release per variant

Live on your management cluster: kyverno-prod, kyverno-test, kyverno-uat. Each variant's profile deploys the same add-ons to the same cluster, and Sveltos lets one profile manage a release at a time, so the per-cluster profiles wait until the live one steps aside. apply also writes takeover.sh, which hands each release over without reinstalling it; run it after apply.sh. See "If your profiles are live" in docs/user/onboard-your-sveltos-fleet.md.

Next: cub sveltos apply <the same input and options> --out <dir>, read <dir>/apply.sh, then run it.

== 0/6 Check before changing anything

== 1/6 One named Target per cluster, in mer-targets

== 2/6 One component, one base and one rollout workflow per profile

== 3/6 One variant per cluster, addressed to that cluster alone

== 4/6 The management cluster's record: its bootstrap profiles

== 5/6 Release each variant, stage by stage: promote, approve, publish

== 6/6 Point Sveltos at ConfigHub (your management cluster)
